{"id": "EUVD-2026-102264", "enisaUuid": "2c49adb7-722b-3c1e-b47a-837c5b73dd76", "description": "libsmi through 0.5.0 contains an out-of-bounds write vulnerability in smiValueAsString() in lib/smi.c that allows attackers to overflow a fixed 1024-byte static buffer through hex rendering of OCTET STRING values. Attackers can supply a crafted MIB with an OCTET STRING DEFVAL of 512 or more octets and a leading 0x00 byte to corrupt adjacent library globals and crash smidump or other consumers.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:10:45", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libsmi-smivalueasstring-octetstring-defval-oob-write", "https://github.com/amartin755/libsmi/blob/c58307210fe995ec419db976eb234aebc71a9216/lib/smi.c#L479-L566", "https://github.com/amartin755/libsmi", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libsmi-through-0.5.0-out-of-bounds-write-via-smivalueasstring-octet-string-defval"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xxf8-vfhv-w73c", "CVE-2026-111137"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1f2c9d18-3970-3556-a7b0-0eb74fa8d5dd", "product": {"name": "libsmi", "vendor": {"name": "Microsoft"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "904b3ce0-1a26-3d03-a19b-d5afe5c07484", "vendor": {"name": "amartin755"}}], "isExploited": false}